# Cliffhangers. A `hook` is the last line of its flight day; its resolver (`due`,
# `when fired <hook>`) opens the next day. The engine spaces hooks >= 4 days apart.
# Resolutions: mostly satisfying, sometimes ominous, never "it was nothing".
# All hooks share hook_who to carry the astronaut over; they never overlap.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# --- 1. The missed knock (late clock) -------------------------------------------
card h_band
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 33 35
weight 60
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
when fired m_flash2
when is A ow_hail
do who hook_who A
text 23:40, mid-window, with Mars square to {A}'s dish. The old-channel carrier misses a knock, the first in-window miss in weeks. {A} counts past eleven, twelve, thirty, out loud now, to an empty cabin, and the next knock doesn't come.

# --- 2. Cabin pressure -------------------------------------------------------
card h_pressure
type event
cat repair
hook
once
days 10 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
do who hook_who A
text The cabin pressure on {A}'s ship is falling, a tenth of a kilopascal an hour. {A} is awake at 01:50 to see it first, a minute before the fleet's night watch.

# --- 3. Solar flare ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flare
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 7 33
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
when !fired storm_shelter
do who hook_who A
text The X-ray monitor jumps at 23:52, and the ground's space weather alert lands minutes later: a major flare. Its protons will reach the fleet in about forty minutes. {A} starts calling the other ships.

# --- 4. Uncommanded thruster --------------------------------------------------
card h_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
do who hook_who A
text 02:14. {A}'s ship starts to roll with nothing in the command log. The control loop fires a thruster. Then another. {A} is already at the console.

card valve_later
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 26 33
roles A
when flag valve_out
when is A valve_who
when since t_valve >= 6
when home A
text Every attitude move on {A}'s ship now takes a beat longer, routed around the valve that was isolated that night. The ground's thruster-select table has a new row with {A}'s initials. {A} has stopped noticing, mostly, except at 02:00.
do morale A -1

# --- 5. Alarm flood -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_flood
type event
cat repair skill
hook
once
days 8 27
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
do who hook_who A
text Just before midnight, 214 alarms hit {A}'s console at once. One of them is real.

# --- 6. Ground silence --------------------------------------------------------
card h_silence
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 10 27
weight 8
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text Mission Control misses a scheduled check-in. Then the next one. {A} sends a third hail and starts the clock: twice the light time, plus a minute for someone to put a coffee down.

# --- 7. Hull strike -----------------------------------------------------------
card h_strike
type event
cat grim
hook
once
days 4 27
weight 9
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
when !is A eva_who
do who hook_who A
text Something hits {A}'s ship hard enough to tick through the whole hull. Every pressure reading is green. {A} reads every green twice, then goes to look.

# --- 8. Star tracker ghost (ominous) ---------------------------------------------
card h_ghost
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 14
roles A
when cond A ok
do who hook_who A
text {A}'s star tracker drops out of lock in the small hours: one star too many in the field, and the next frame doesn't agree with the first. Attitude hands over to the backup tracker, which has never been asked to fly alone.

# --- 9. A voice on the loop ----------------------------------------------------------
card h_voice
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 25 33
weight 10
roles A
when cond A ok
when home A
do who hook_who A
text 02:40. The intercom on {A}'s ship opens and plays four seconds of a kitchen somewhere: a kettle, a radio, someone laughing. The intercom's clock reads tomorrow.

# --- 10. A ship drops off the net -------------------------------------------------
card h_dark
type event
cat mystery
hook
once
days 26 31
weight 90
roles A
when cond A ok
when !is A ow_hail
when since t_frame >= 1
when home A
do who hook_who A
text 23:58. {A}'s ship stops answering on the fleet net in the middle of a sentence. No telemetry, just an empty slot on seven displays. Through the next ship's long lens, its cabin windows are lit as usual.

